      "math_academy_id": "e-3978",
      "problem": "The equation $\\log_3{9} = 2$ is equivalent to $b^2 = 9.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\log_{b}{a} = x$ is equivalent to $a = b^x$\n\nIf we compare $\\log_3{9} = 2$ with $\\log_{b}{a} = x,$ we get $a = 9,$ $b = 3,$ and $x = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to $3^2 = 9.$ Consequently, $b = 3.$",
